designs.seasonModel:
SEASON AS FIRST-CLASS ENTITY (lightweight, corrects winter-sport mis-bucketing):

SCHEMA (additive, nullable — backward-compatible):
  Season {
    id: UUID
    tenantId: FK Tenant (cascade)
    sport: string (e.g. "BASKETBALL", "FOOTBALL")
    year: string (e.g. "2025-26" academic year, or "2026" calendar year for spring sports)
    label: string (e.g. "2025-26 Varsity Basketball", "2026 Track & Field")
    startDate: DateTime (e.g. Sept 1, 2025 for HS fall/winter)
    endDate: DateTime (e.g. June 30, 2026 for HS winter/spring)
    createdAt: DateTime
    updatedAt: DateTime

    @@unique([tenantId, sport, year])
    @@index([tenantId, sport])
  }

SOFT REFERENCES (no strict FK, allows gradual adoption):
  - Game.season: nullable string (e.g. "2025-26"), set at game-create via operator-picked Team.season or sensible default (see deriveSeason fix above).
  - Team.season: nullable string (e.g. "2025-26"), set at team creation (Varsity Basketball → "2025-26").
  - PlayerSeasonStat.season: already exists as string, populated by finalizeGameStats(deriveSeason(game)).

DERIVATION (fixes calendar-year split):
  ```typescript
  function deriveSeason(game: { startedAt?: Date | null; createdAt?: Date | null }, sport?: string): string {
    const d = game.startedAt ?? game.createdAt ?? new Date();
    if (!(d instanceof Date) || Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return String(new Date().getFullYear());

    const month = d.getMonth(); // 0-11
    const year = d.getFullYear();

    // Winter sports (Sept-Mar): emit "YYYY-YY" (next calendar year's 2-digit suffix).
    // Spring sports (Apr-Aug): emit "YYYY" (calendar year).
    // Heuristic: if month >= 8 (Sept+), next school year; else this calendar year.
    if (month >= 8) {
      return `${year}-${String(year + 1).slice(-2)}`;
    } else {
      return `${year - 1}-${String(year).slice(-2)}`;
    }
  }
  ```
  - Stable: same game always derives same season (finalize + re-finalize converge).
  - Backward-compatible: existing bare-year PlayerSeasonStat rows stay as-is (no migration needed for pilot); new rows use "YYYY-YY".

UI (minimal, operator sets once per team):
  - Team creation / edit: optional dropdown "Academic Season" → "2025-26", "2024-25", or "Auto-detect (from game date)".
  - Defaults to "Auto-detect" (deriveSeason logic).
  - When operator picks explicit season, Game.season inherited from Team.season at game-create time.

LEADERBOARD SCOPING:
  - GET /api/v1/sports/leaders?sport=BASKETBALL&statKey=PTS&scope=SEASON&season=2025-26 (existing, unchanged; season is already a query param).
  - Backend filters PlayerSeasonStat WHERE season = '2025-26' (exact match).
  - If ?season omitted, returns all-seasons aggregate (current fallback).

BACKFILL (one-time, safe for pilot):
  - If pilot has existing games already finalized with bare-year seasons ("2026"):
    1. Inspect game.startedAt month; if Sept-Mar, move PlayerSeasonStat rows from season="2026" to season="2025-26" (or delete + re-finalize).
    2. Or accept existing split and just start fresh with new games using fixed deriveSeason. No breakage (old + new leaderboards coexist).

designs.finalizeWiring:
1. ALREADY WIRED (Verified):
   – finalizeGameStats() is called in sports.service.ts:3344, post-FINAL status transition.
   – Wrapped in try/catch (fail-open, non-fatal).
   – Gated by FLAGS.SPORTS_PLAYER_STATS (operator/tenant can opt-in).
   – Idempotent: checks stats[STATS_FINALIZED_MARKER] to skip re-finalize.
   – Only aggregates LINKED rows (personId not null) on OUR-team (isHome=true).
   – Respects stat semantics: counting stats roll up, rate stats stay per-game.

2. REQUIRED FIXES (P0 Correctness):

   a) Fix deriveSeason() in sports-stats.service.ts:414
      Current: returns String(year) e.g. '2026' (calendar year)
      Problem: Winter sports straddle Jan 1 → splits a basketball season into two rows.
      Fix:
        export function deriveSeason(game: {
          startedAt?: Date | null;
          createdAt?: Date | null;
          season?: string | null;  // ADD
        }): string {
          // If Game.season is set (e.g. '2025-26'), use it
          if (game.season) return game.season;

          // Else derive from calendar year as fallback
          const d = game.startedAt ?? game.createdAt ?? new Date();
          const year = d instanceof Date && !isNaN(d.getTime())
            ? d.getFullYear()
            : new Date().getFullYear();
          return String(year);
        }
      – Also add optional Game.season column (nullable string, no index) for future explicit assignment.

   b) Wire linkRosterPlayerToPerson() at ROSTER IMPORT (not per-game manual link)
      Current: RosterPanel shows LinkAthleteButton (manual, per-game, per-player, per-tap).
      Problem: Operator must re-link every player every game (impossible at scale).
      Fix: In roster-import.ts (or sports.service.ts::importRoster):
        for (const row of csvRows) {
          const personId = await linkRosterPlayerToPerson(prisma, {
            tenantId, 
            rosterPlayerId: row.id,
            fullName: row.name,
            teamId: team.id,  // NOW we have a persistent Team!
          });
          // Link is done; don't need the button later.
        }
      – Result: RosterPlayer.personId is set at import time. LinkAthleteButton removed.

3. ECHO LINKED STATE BACK TO CLIENT (UX clarity):
   – Current: LinkAthleteButton sets local state `setLinked(true)` but refresh clears it (no DB readback).
   – Fix: Include linkedPersonId in roster GET response. Client can render 'Linked' icon without one-tap.
   – This is a polish; not critical if we remove the button entirely at import-time linking.

"
